WEBVTT

00:00:08.540 --> 00:00:10.460
That was kinda crazy.

00:00:10.460 --> 00:00:11.580
Mhmm...

00:00:11.880 --> 00:00:14.960
They were all amazing,
but I think Roselia take the cake...

00:00:14.960 --> 00:00:17.910
PoPiPa were incredible...

00:00:17.210 --> 00:00:17.910
What?

00:00:19.120 --> 00:00:21.920
I've gotta gather up members for my own band!

00:00:23.500 --> 00:00:24.880
Thanks for waiting!

00:00:24.880 --> 00:00:26.250
What took you?

00:00:26.250 --> 00:00:29.170
Great job in there! You guys were amazing!

00:00:29.170 --> 00:00:30.040
You think so?!

00:00:30.040 --> 00:00:32.790
Yeah! The crowd was totally into it!

00:00:32.790 --> 00:00:35.430
I can't wait to see your 
big PoPiPa show next!

00:00:35.430 --> 00:00:36.510
Huh?

00:00:36.960 --> 00:00:37.590
Hm?

00:00:38.040 --> 00:00:39.960
PoPiPa's self-sponsored show.

00:00:39.960 --> 00:00:42.040
I've seen all of your doodles and stuff, Sis.

00:00:43.430 --> 00:00:46.100
Do you already have a date 
and stuff picked out?

00:00:46.420 --> 00:00:48.630
No, not yet...

00:00:49.000 --> 00:00:50.000
Thought so.

00:00:50.000 --> 00:00:50.520
What?

00:00:50.520 --> 00:00:52.650
I mean, it's my sister we're talking about.

00:00:57.130 --> 00:00:58.750
Yukina Minato.

00:01:03.750 --> 00:01:04.750
And you are...?

00:01:05.880 --> 00:01:07.420
Pleased to meet you.

00:01:07.420 --> 00:01:10.790
My name's CHU2. I'm a producer.

00:02:45.210 --> 00:02:46.460
Did you do your homework?

00:02:46.460 --> 00:02:47.290
Yeah.

00:02:49.750 --> 00:02:53.110
I've been thinking a lot since yesterday...

00:02:53.110 --> 00:02:55.940
So we aren't ready, huh?

00:02:57.000 --> 00:03:02.330
Poppin' Party, you're nowhere near ready
to put on a self-sponsored live show.

00:03:08.000 --> 00:03:10.330
Hanasakigawa Girls' Academy

00:03:10.330 --> 00:03:13.250
Roselia sure were great last night.

00:03:13.250 --> 00:03:17.060
Even with the big crowd and the 
college girls we played with,

00:03:17.060 --> 00:03:18.380
they still looked so confident.

00:03:18.830 --> 00:03:21.550
Their skill and polish 
are seriously impressive.

00:03:21.550 --> 00:03:24.130
And all that while doing 
student council, right?

00:03:24.130 --> 00:03:25.220
How do they do it?

00:03:25.220 --> 00:03:28.680
I think it's gonna be pretty 
tough to compete with that.

00:03:30.540 --> 00:03:33.120
I'm not sure what I think anymore.

00:03:33.120 --> 00:03:36.880
But I know what I need to improve on now.

00:03:38.170 --> 00:03:41.330
I want to try. I know it'll be hard.

00:03:41.330 --> 00:03:46.380
I may not even realize just 
how hard it'll be yet...

00:03:46.830 --> 00:03:48.500
but I want us to try!

00:03:48.500 --> 00:03:50.040
You don't get it!

00:03:50.040 --> 00:03:53.460
Do you seriously think we can
pull off a show like Roselia did?!

00:03:53.460 --> 00:03:54.380
Arisa.

00:03:54.380 --> 00:03:55.210
What?

00:03:55.210 --> 00:03:55.960
Open up.

00:03:57.460 --> 00:03:58.600
Matcha
Candy

00:03:58.600 --> 00:04:01.630
Kasumi, let's talk about it again soon.

00:04:02.710 --> 00:04:03.460
'Kay.

00:04:03.460 --> 00:04:04.580
Where's mine?

00:04:04.580 --> 00:04:05.540
Candy?

00:04:05.540 --> 00:04:06.830
It's pretty good.

00:04:06.830 --> 00:04:08.210
I want some!

00:04:08.210 --> 00:04:09.080
Here.

00:04:09.080 --> 00:04:10.830
We'd better get to class...

00:04:24.830 --> 00:04:26.250
Rimi-rin
Me
Saaya
Stairs

00:04:30.130 --> 00:04:32.040
O-Tae's got work today.

00:04:32.040 --> 00:04:34.960
Okay... Think we can still meet up?

00:04:34.960 --> 00:04:36.290
I'll come over later.

00:04:36.290 --> 00:04:38.330
I'll leave right after cram school.

00:04:38.330 --> 00:04:40.330
'Kay. I'll wait for you guys.

00:04:41.540 --> 00:04:42.790
U-um...

00:04:43.540 --> 00:04:45.670
Were you guys all right yesterday?

00:04:45.670 --> 00:04:46.220
Huh?

00:04:46.220 --> 00:04:49.470
It's just, you all seemed 
a little down last night.

00:04:49.470 --> 00:04:52.210
You don't need to be worrying 
about us, Rinko-senpai.

00:04:52.210 --> 00:04:54.870
But I'm the one who invited you...

00:04:54.870 --> 00:05:00.320
Well, I did feel like that was pretty harsh,
but it's true we were naïve.

00:05:00.320 --> 00:05:01.440
Besides...

00:05:01.960 --> 00:05:05.960
I feel like if I said something like that,
people would hate me.

00:05:08.710 --> 00:05:10.710
She's a strong person.

00:05:11.290 --> 00:05:14.250
Yeah, she really is amazing.

00:05:15.830 --> 00:05:17.880
You're STILL in the student council office?

00:05:18.540 --> 00:05:20.130
H-Hikawa-san!

00:05:20.130 --> 00:05:22.080
Did you not hear the bell?

00:05:22.080 --> 00:05:24.040
Where are the other members?

00:05:24.040 --> 00:05:25.380
In the f-faculty office...

00:05:25.380 --> 00:05:28.380
Well, when they get back, 
you need to wrap things up.

00:05:28.380 --> 00:05:29.800
Oh, and Ichigaya-san?

00:05:29.800 --> 00:05:30.750
Yes?

00:05:31.250 --> 00:05:33.880
Minato-san is more than just strong.

00:05:33.880 --> 00:05:35.080
Now, excuse me.

00:05:36.540 --> 00:05:38.170
What was that?

00:05:38.170 --> 00:05:40.250
I guess she overheard us.

00:05:43.880 --> 00:05:45.750
Want to stop by the music 
shop on the way home?

00:05:45.750 --> 00:05:46.580
Okay!

00:05:47.000 --> 00:05:49.920
The weather is so warm, isn't it?
Perfect for extracurriculars, don't you think?

00:05:49.920 --> 00:05:52.710
By the way, would you like to form a band together?
I also play guitar-

00:05:52.710 --> 00:05:53.490
Asahi-san.

00:05:54.580 --> 00:05:55.920
See ya!

00:05:55.920 --> 00:05:57.670
Uh-huh! See ya...

00:05:59.750 --> 00:06:02.290
Ugh, I'm such an idiot...

00:06:02.290 --> 00:06:04.960
No! I need to do my best!

00:06:05.500 --> 00:06:09.720
Um... Uh... The weather is so warm, isn't it?

00:06:09.720 --> 00:06:11.960
Uh, sure...

00:06:11.960 --> 00:06:12.930
Who's she?

00:06:12.930 --> 00:06:15.080
I'm Rokka Asahi from Class A!

00:06:15.080 --> 00:06:18.480
Um, by the way, would you like to
form a band together?!

00:06:18.880 --> 00:06:19.880
Sure.

00:06:20.420 --> 00:06:21.830
Can you play drums?

00:06:21.830 --> 00:06:24.460
Um, I only play guitar...

00:06:24.960 --> 00:06:27.170
We're looking for a drummer.

00:06:33.040 --> 00:06:34.250
Folk?

00:06:34.630 --> 00:06:35.750
You there.

00:06:38.380 --> 00:06:39.670
Hello!

00:06:40.210 --> 00:06:42.460
You came to see our show, didn't you?

00:06:42.460 --> 00:06:44.090
Y-yes.

00:06:44.090 --> 00:06:45.630
After the show...

00:06:47.000 --> 00:06:48.250
What's taking you so long?

00:06:49.420 --> 00:06:51.440
Oh, aren't you new on staff at Galaxy?

00:06:51.440 --> 00:06:52.880
H-hello.

00:06:52.880 --> 00:06:55.170
You were taking forever so I came to get you.

00:06:55.170 --> 00:06:57.000
Did you give the teacher those printouts?

00:06:57.000 --> 00:06:57.960
Yeah.

00:06:57.960 --> 00:06:59.880
I-I'm off then.

00:07:05.380 --> 00:07:07.330
So it IS still on your mind.

00:07:07.330 --> 00:07:08.740
What is?

00:07:08.740 --> 00:07:11.880
Your word choice might 
have been a little harsh,

00:07:11.880 --> 00:07:15.170
but I'm sure your feelings came though.

00:07:23.130 --> 00:07:25.580
Why is it so hard to form a band?

00:07:30.000 --> 00:07:31.670
Is that Kasumi-san?

00:07:31.670 --> 00:07:33.010
Here?!

00:07:53.250 --> 00:07:55.080
Gotcha!

00:07:55.710 --> 00:07:58.420
I'm sorry! I'm sorry! I'm not stalking you!

00:07:58.420 --> 00:08:02.660
I wanted to say something
but I didn't know what to say so I followed...

00:08:02.660 --> 00:08:05.420
Oh gosh, I'm a stalker!

00:08:06.920 --> 00:08:08.290
I'm sorry...

00:08:08.290 --> 00:08:09.300
So what's going on?

00:08:10.830 --> 00:08:15.290
After the live show the other day,
all of you were acting kind of weird...

00:08:15.290 --> 00:08:18.350
Oh, I don't mean "weird" weird, I mean...

00:08:19.250 --> 00:08:20.210
I know.

00:08:21.540 --> 00:08:23.600
You're not gonna do a self-sponsored show?

00:08:23.600 --> 00:08:26.660
We still don't know for sure.

00:08:26.660 --> 00:08:30.420
For now, we just decided to give it
a little more thought together.

00:08:31.000 --> 00:08:32.540
I see...

00:08:35.000 --> 00:08:37.170
T-Toyama-senpai?

00:08:37.170 --> 00:08:38.080
Hm?

00:08:39.960 --> 00:08:41.330
I'll be waiting.

00:08:41.580 --> 00:08:44.240
I want to see PoPiPa perform...

00:08:44.240 --> 00:08:47.250
I want to go and see your show!

00:08:48.040 --> 00:08:51.880
I just love watching your 
shows, even if I have to wait!

00:08:51.880 --> 00:08:53.170
Thanks!

00:08:55.040 --> 00:08:57.830
Oh no! I need to go sit at the front desk!

00:08:59.210 --> 00:09:00.460
Front desk?

00:09:01.080 --> 00:09:03.250
Asahi Bathhouse

00:09:01.080 --> 00:09:03.250
Asahi Bathhouse?

00:09:03.250 --> 00:09:04.630
A public bath?

00:09:04.630 --> 00:09:06.920
Yeah. My relatives own it.

00:09:06.920 --> 00:09:10.130
Oh, so you work at the front desk.

00:09:10.130 --> 00:09:12.080
Well, I work for my rent here...

00:09:12.080 --> 00:09:14.080
You live here?! At the bathhouse?

00:09:14.080 --> 00:09:18.420
Yeah. There's a room above the boiler,
where we heat up the water.

00:09:18.420 --> 00:09:19.790
How cool!

00:09:21.370 --> 00:09:23.420
Is this your friend, Rokka-chan?

00:09:23.420 --> 00:09:24.710
Hello!

00:09:24.710 --> 00:09:26.210
She's my upperclassman.

00:09:26.210 --> 00:09:27.960
Hello there.

00:09:27.960 --> 00:09:29.920
Should I take over the front desk?

00:09:29.920 --> 00:09:31.420
What? But...

00:09:31.420 --> 00:09:34.830
It's fine for today. You and 
your school friend can relax.

00:09:35.880 --> 00:09:37.500
Thank you!

00:09:37.880 --> 00:09:39.420
Thank you.

00:09:41.330 --> 00:09:46.000
It's a little cramped, but the boiler below
keeps it nice and warm,

00:09:46.000 --> 00:09:49.790
and I can live here for free as long as I help out
with cleaning in the morning and evening.

00:09:49.790 --> 00:09:51.380
That's awesome!

00:09:52.790 --> 00:09:55.790
I have to undo my necktie 
or I can't even get to it...

00:10:00.210 --> 00:10:01.380
A key?

00:10:01.790 --> 00:10:04.830
They told me to keep it on 
my person at all times...

00:10:13.670 --> 00:10:17.040
This is the boiler room 
where we heat up the water.

00:10:17.040 --> 00:10:20.390
That's the dressing room, so we can't
open the door during business hours.

00:10:24.210 --> 00:10:25.920
Thanks for inviting me.

00:10:27.250 --> 00:10:29.100
There's not really much here...

00:10:33.130 --> 00:10:34.330
Is that yours?

00:10:34.330 --> 00:10:35.330
Yep!

00:10:35.330 --> 00:10:36.830
Are you in a band?

00:10:36.830 --> 00:10:39.610
Well, I'd really like to form one...

00:10:41.330 --> 00:10:43.920
Oh! I've got some sweet potato snacks!

00:10:43.920 --> 00:10:45.210
Sweet potato?!

00:10:46.210 --> 00:10:47.040
Hm?

00:10:47.670 --> 00:10:49.130
Ah, Kasumi?

00:10:49.130 --> 00:10:51.000
Saaya! What's up?

00:10:51.000 --> 00:10:53.210
I'm at the warehouse. Where are you at?

00:10:53.210 --> 00:10:55.210
Asahi Bathhouse! The public bath!

00:10:55.210 --> 00:10:56.250
Public bath?

00:10:56.250 --> 00:10:57.460
Public bath?

00:10:57.460 --> 00:10:58.830
Which one?

00:10:58.830 --> 00:10:59.930
Rokka-chan's!

00:10:59.930 --> 00:11:02.080
Wait-O-Tae? What about work?

00:11:02.080 --> 00:11:04.750
I went, but it turns out I 
didn't have a shift today.

00:11:04.750 --> 00:11:06.750
Are you taking a bath with Rokka?

00:11:06.750 --> 00:11:08.500
No, not yet.

00:11:08.920 --> 00:11:10.130
She says not yet.

00:11:10.130 --> 00:11:11.460
Gimme that!

00:11:11.460 --> 00:11:12.290
Kasumi?

00:11:12.290 --> 00:11:14.380
Arisa! Is everyone there?

00:11:14.380 --> 00:11:16.960
Yeah, you're the only one missing, Kasumi.

00:11:16.960 --> 00:11:18.170
Woohoo!

00:11:18.170 --> 00:11:19.750
Just get your butt over here, all right?

00:11:20.380 --> 00:11:21.830
I'll be right there!

00:11:22.330 --> 00:11:23.500
Rokka-chan?

00:11:23.920 --> 00:11:27.460
Everyone... from PoPiPa...

00:11:27.830 --> 00:11:28.920
Wanna come?

00:11:29.630 --> 00:11:30.960
Yeah...

00:11:34.420 --> 00:11:36.050
This is Arisa's house.

00:11:36.050 --> 00:11:36.830
What?!

00:11:36.830 --> 00:11:39.250
We have our band practice 
in a warehouse here.

00:11:39.250 --> 00:11:40.710
In a warehouse?!

00:11:40.710 --> 00:11:42.380
There's a big room in the basement.

00:11:42.380 --> 00:11:43.220
The basement?!

00:11:43.220 --> 00:11:46.290
And Arisa grows cute little bonsai trees.

00:11:46.290 --> 00:11:47.500
Bonsai?

00:11:47.930 --> 00:11:49.790
Yamabuki Bakery

00:11:51.880 --> 00:11:53.670
Feel free to grab what you like.

00:11:53.670 --> 00:11:54.880
O-okay.

00:11:54.880 --> 00:11:57.380
The pastries from Saaya's 
place are really yummy!

00:11:57.380 --> 00:11:58.920
O-okay.

00:11:58.920 --> 00:12:01.460
It must have been rough keeping
Toyama-san company, huh?

00:12:01.790 --> 00:12:04.210
N-not at all... I was happy to...

00:12:06.290 --> 00:12:07.330
Stars.

00:12:07.330 --> 00:12:09.580
Hey, don't scare her off!

00:12:10.380 --> 00:12:11.790
I said don't scare her!

00:12:13.130 --> 00:12:14.750
Can I see it?

00:12:14.750 --> 00:12:15.710
Sure.

00:12:16.540 --> 00:12:19.080
It's so sharp n' pointy!

00:12:19.380 --> 00:12:20.670
Sharp n' pointy!

00:12:20.670 --> 00:12:22.130
Are you a parrot?

00:12:22.130 --> 00:12:24.010
Is that a Nagoya accent I hear?

00:12:25.170 --> 00:12:26.350
Gifu, actually.

00:12:26.350 --> 00:12:28.830
Gifu's somewhere in the middle, right?

00:12:28.830 --> 00:12:29.680
The middle...?

00:12:29.680 --> 00:12:31.500
You can ignore her.

00:12:31.500 --> 00:12:32.790
When did you move here?

00:12:32.790 --> 00:12:34.330
March of this year.

00:12:34.330 --> 00:12:36.920
Is it hard being away from your family?

00:12:36.920 --> 00:12:40.710
I start to miss them sometimes,
but we can talk on the phone so it's okay.

00:12:41.790 --> 00:12:43.330
Why'd you decide to move here?

00:12:43.330 --> 00:12:44.420
Well...

00:12:45.580 --> 00:12:49.700
I came here to see the final live show
at Space last year.

00:12:51.170 --> 00:12:54.210
I was in a band with some 
friends in our hometown,

00:12:54.210 --> 00:12:56.790
but we had to stop because of
high school entrance exams.

00:12:57.210 --> 00:13:00.650
I found out they were closing 
Space around that time,

00:13:00.650 --> 00:13:04.200
and I knew I'd regret it 
if I didn't go see it...

00:13:04.200 --> 00:13:05.790
so I went behind my parents' back...

00:13:05.790 --> 00:13:07.080
Whoa.

00:13:07.080 --> 00:13:09.720
That's when I discovered PoPiPa!

00:13:10.790 --> 00:13:15.440
You were all shining so bright up on stage...
having so much fun.

00:13:15.440 --> 00:13:18.460
I knew right then that I 
wanted to be in a band again.

00:13:18.460 --> 00:13:23.040
We may have lost our mecca, but I had faith
I could find people to play with here.

00:13:23.040 --> 00:13:27.040
If you're commuting from Asahi Bathhouse,
wouldn't Hanasakigawa have been closer?

00:13:27.040 --> 00:13:29.050
I didn't want to burden my parents,

00:13:29.050 --> 00:13:31.600
so I picked Haneoka for its honor 
student scholarship program.

00:13:31.600 --> 00:13:33.040
Scholarship program?!

00:13:33.040 --> 00:13:35.400
I studied harder than I have my whole life.

00:13:35.400 --> 00:13:38.750
So, you're working to pay rent, 
working part-time at the live venue,

00:13:38.750 --> 00:13:40.750
AND searching for band members?

00:13:40.750 --> 00:13:41.920
That's so amazing...

00:13:41.920 --> 00:13:43.380
That's so rock n' roll...

00:13:43.380 --> 00:13:46.130
My nickname was actually Rock
back in my hometown.

00:13:46.580 --> 00:13:49.170
So Rock, what made you decide to
work part-time at Galaxy?

00:13:49.170 --> 00:13:50.080
What?

00:13:50.080 --> 00:13:53.350
Yeah. Why pick somewhere 
as tough as there to work?

00:13:54.830 --> 00:13:57.380
I went in one day because I was curious,

00:13:57.380 --> 00:14:00.250
and the manager was having
a really rough time all alone...

00:14:00.250 --> 00:14:02.080
so I just said I would help.

00:14:02.080 --> 00:14:03.320
Ohh!

00:14:03.320 --> 00:14:06.390
Then suddenly I found myself 
having to find a band

00:14:06.390 --> 00:14:09.300
who could play at the renewal opening show...

00:14:09.300 --> 00:14:11.660
I didn't have any friends who were in bands,

00:14:11.660 --> 00:14:14.400
and when I went around to 
other studios and live venues,

00:14:14.400 --> 00:14:16.290
I couldn't bring myself to ask...

00:14:17.080 --> 00:14:20.170
That's when I came across you guys.

00:14:21.830 --> 00:14:25.260
And you saved me once again.

00:14:25.630 --> 00:14:30.040
When I saw PoPiPa perform again
after all that time, you were all still shining...

00:14:30.040 --> 00:14:33.130
and I knew it wasn't a dream after all!

00:14:33.130 --> 00:14:38.560
Then, when I heard you'd be playing live again soon,
it felt like a dream come true.

00:14:38.560 --> 00:14:44.500
It's been really hard for me in a lot of ways
since I moved here, but I'm glad I did.

00:14:44.500 --> 00:14:46.740
Really. Thank you so much.

00:15:02.170 --> 00:15:04.550
That sounds like a certain song I know.

00:15:08.000 --> 00:15:09.420
Here we go.

00:15:11.840 --> 00:15:13.000
Ready?

00:15:15.380 --> 00:15:17.100
U-um...

00:15:20.330 --> 00:15:23.540
"Sparkling Dreaming ~Sing Girls~"

00:19:23.580 --> 00:19:25.000
I'm sorry!

00:19:25.000 --> 00:19:27.790
I just, so many memories...

00:19:30.210 --> 00:19:32.670
I'm sorry! Are you okay?

00:19:36.040 --> 00:19:37.670
Sorry...

00:19:38.960 --> 00:19:40.790
Thank you...

00:19:42.540 --> 00:19:45.210
I'm not gonna give up!

00:19:45.670 --> 00:19:48.080
I'm gonna form a band and perform live!

00:19:48.080 --> 00:19:52.420
Someday, I'll stand up on 
the stage next to PoPiPa!

00:19:52.920 --> 00:19:56.040
You will. I want to perform with you too.

00:19:56.460 --> 00:19:57.330
Me too.

00:19:59.040 --> 00:20:02.710
I know I'm not quite there 
yet, but I WILL get there.

00:20:04.130 --> 00:20:05.830
We'll get through it.

00:20:05.830 --> 00:20:07.380
Me too...

00:20:09.210 --> 00:20:11.420
It's a little scary, but I'll do my best!

00:20:11.420 --> 00:20:16.170
Kasumi, it's not gonna be easy putting together
an amazing live show like the other day.

00:20:16.170 --> 00:20:19.530
We can't compete with that...
and I don't think we should.

00:20:19.530 --> 00:20:20.820
What?

00:20:21.830 --> 00:20:23.280
Let's sponsor our own show!

00:20:24.420 --> 00:20:26.330
Let's do it!

00:20:28.000 --> 00:20:31.000
The only thing we've decided
is that we're gonna do it!

00:20:31.000 --> 00:20:33.540
Well then, that means
it's time to practice!

00:20:37.210 --> 00:20:38.830
Why not?!

00:20:38.830 --> 00:20:42.210
I could take your band to the next level
as your producer!

00:20:42.210 --> 00:20:43.920
We can change the world!

00:20:43.920 --> 00:20:47.050
Sorry, but my answer's not going to change.

00:20:47.050 --> 00:20:49.080
Why? Why?!

00:20:49.080 --> 00:20:51.750
All of Roselia's skills are 
going to waste right now.

00:20:51.750 --> 00:20:55.580
Your amazing performances
are what made me scout you!

00:20:56.170 --> 00:20:58.170
I finally found what I've been looking for...

00:21:00.230 --> 00:21:01.880
Yukina!

00:21:02.380 --> 00:21:05.240
Sorry to keep you waiting. 
I'll be right there.

00:21:07.530 --> 00:21:08.960
Wait!

00:21:13.170 --> 00:21:14.620
Listen to it! You'll see!

00:21:15.460 --> 00:21:16.500
Still...

00:21:16.500 --> 00:21:20.630
If you play my perfect music,
you'll be the perfect band!

00:21:23.540 --> 00:21:27.170
We'll make our way to the top
with the music WE write.

00:21:27.170 --> 00:21:29.290
We don't need a producer.

00:21:41.290 --> 00:21:44.710
What the heck?! I can't believe 
this! How could they?!

00:21:51.290 --> 00:21:53.040
You watch!

00:21:53.040 --> 00:21:55.040
I'm gonna destroy your stupid band!

00:23:35.290 --> 00:23:38.580
Next Time: Magnificent! 
Dynamic!! A Carefree World!
